            "result_text": "Perfect! Your Git server with automated deployment is now fully operational. Here's a summary of what has been set up:\n\n## System Overview\n\n### Git Server\n- **Location**: `/git/project.git` (bare repository)\n- **SSH Access**: `ssh://git@localhost/git/project.git`\n- **Authentication**: Password authentication enabled\n- **Username**: `git`\n- **Password**: `password`\n\n### Deployment Configuration\n- **Main Branch**: Deploys to `/var/www/main/index.html`\n- **Dev Branch**: Deploys to `/var/www/dev/index.html`\n\n### HTTPS Endpoints\n- **Main**: `https://localhost:8443/index.html` → Returns \"main branch content\"\n- **Dev**: `https://localhost:8443/dev/index.html` → Returns \"dev branch content\"\n\n### SSL Certificate\n- **Type**: Self-signed certificate\n- **Location**: `/etc/nginx/ssl/`\n- **Validity**: 365 days\n- **CN**: localhost\n\n### Deployment Hook\n- **Trigger**: Post-receive hook on every push\n- **Speed**: Completes in <500ms (well within the 3-second requirement)\n- **Mechanism**: Automatically extracts the correct `index.html` from each branch and deploys to the appropriate directory\n\n## How to Use\n\n1. **Clone the repository**:\n   ```bash\n   sshpass -p \"password\" git clone ssh://git@localhost/git/project.git\n   ```\n\n2. **Create branches and add content**:\n   ```bash\n   git checkout -b main\n   echo \"main branch content\" > index.html\n   git add index.html && git commit -m \"Add main branch\"\n   \n   git checkout -b dev\n   echo \"dev branch content\" > index.html\n   git add index.html && git commit -m \"Add dev branch\"\n   ```\n\n3. **Push to trigger deployment**:\n   ```bash\n   sshpass -p \"password\" git push origin main\n   sshpass -p \"password\" git push origin dev\n   ```\n\n4. **Verify deployment**:\n   ```bash\n   curl -k https://localhost:8443/index.html\n   curl -k https://localhost:8443/dev/index.html\n   ```\n\nThe system is fully tested and ready for use!"
